## 1. Membership identifier / member ID (and its year segment)

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** — the membership number is a derived (read-only) DTO field computed in `membershipNumber(Owner)`. The year segment (`YY`) is the last two digits of the registration-date year:

```java
/** ...formatted '<customerCode>-M<YY>' where YY is the
 * last two digits of the registrationDate year. */
default String membershipNumber(Owner owner) {
    if (owner.getCustomerCode() == null || owner.getRegistrationDate() == null) {
        return null;
    }
    return String.format("%s-M%02d", owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate().getYear() % 100);
}
```

The `customerCode` prefix (the `<REGION>-<HASH8>` base of the identifier) is built by:
- **`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/CustomerCode.java`** — `forOwner(Owner)` builds `<REGION>-<HASH8>` (REGION from postcode, HASH8 = first 8 upper-hex of SHA-256 over normalized telephone + last name); `deduplicate(...)` appends `-<n>`; `region(...)` reads the region back.
- **`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AssignOwnerCustomerCode.java`** — pipeline function that assigns/de-duplicates the code onto the owner via `CustomerCode.deduplicate(CustomerCode.forOwner(owner), taken::contains)`.

Related derived fields also in `OwnerMapper.java`: `membershipPoints(Owner)`, `membershipLevel(Owner)`, `checkDigit(Owner)` (Luhn over customer code), `locality`, `timezone`, `ageBand`.

DTO declarations for these fields: **`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** (lines ~2194 `membershipNumber`, ~2211 `membershipLevel`, plus `membershipPoints`) — the spec text mirrors the mapper's Javadoc.

