## 3. Business-day adjustment of the registration date

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/BusinessDays.java`** — the single definition of the roll-forward, skipping weekends and a fixed 2026 holiday set:

```java
private static final Set<LocalDate> HOLIDAYS = Set.of(
        LocalDate.parse("2026-01-01"), LocalDate.parse("2026-01-26"),
        LocalDate.parse("2026-04-25"), LocalDate.parse("2026-12-25"), LocalDate.parse("2026-12-28"));

static LocalDate rollForward(LocalDate date) {
    while (isWeekend(date) || HOLIDAYS.contains(date)) {
        date = date.plusDays(1);
    }
    return date;
}
```

Registration-date pipeline (order matters):
- **`.../owner/RejectFutureRegistrationDate.java`** — rejects a supplied date after today (400) *before* any roll-forward.
- **`.../owner/ResolveOwnerRegistrationDate.java`** — picks supplied-or-today and applies `BusinessDays.rollForward(...)`, publishing the resolved `LocalDate`.
- **`.../owner/ApplyOwnerRegistrationDate.java`** — stamps the built `Owner` with that resolved business-day date, so every derived value (including the membership number's year segment) uses the adjusted date.
- **`.../owner/RejectDailyOwnerLimit.java`** — caps registrations per business day (`DAILY_LIMIT = 100`) using the resolved date.
- **`.../owner/OwnerRegistrationDays.java`** — `size(owners, date)` counts owners registered on an exact date; shared by the daily-limit and bulk-signup rules.

