## 2. Tenure (year / 365-day windows)

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Tenure.java`** — the single definition of tenure as whole days since registration, floored at 0 for null/future dates:

```java
public static long days(LocalDate registrationDate) {
    if (registrationDate == null) {
        return 0;
    }
    return Math.max(ChronoUnit.DAYS.between(registrationDate, LocalDate.now()), 0);
}
```

Consumed by `OwnerMapper.membershipPoints(...)` — `if (Tenure.days(owner.getRegistrationDate()) > 365) { points += 3; }` — the 365-day window.

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/AgeBand.java`** — a related whole-years computation (`Period.between(birthDate, registrationDate).getYears()`) mapping to `MINOR`/`ADULT`/`SENIOR`, used by `OwnerMapper.ageBand(...)`.

---

## 3. Business-day adjustment of the registration date

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/BusinessDays.java`** — the single definition of the roll-forward, skipping weekends and a fixed 2026 holiday set:

```java
private static final Set<LocalDate> HOLIDAYS = Set.of(
        LocalDate.parse("2026-01-01"), LocalDate.parse("2026-01-26"),
        LocalDate.parse("2026-04-25"), LocalDate.parse("2026-12-25"), LocalDate.parse("2026-12-28"));

static LocalDate rollForward(LocalDate date) {
    while (isWeekend(date) || HOLIDAYS.contains(date)) {
        date = date.plusDays(1);
    }
    return date;
}
```

Registration-date pipeline (order matters):
- **`.../owner/RejectFutureRegistrationDate.java`** — rejects a supplied date after today (400) *before* any roll-forward.
- **`.../owner/ResolveOwnerRegistrationDate.java`** — picks supplied-or-today and applies `BusinessDays.rollForward(...)`, publishing the resolved `LocalDate`.
- **`.../owner/ApplyOwnerRegistrationDate.java`** — stamps the built `Owner` with that resolved business-day date, so every derived value (including the membership number's year segment) uses the adjusted date.
- **`.../owner/RejectDailyOwnerLimit.java`** — caps registrations per business day (`DAILY_LIMIT = 100`) using the resolved date.
- **`.../owner/OwnerRegistrationDays.java`** — `size(owners, date)` counts owners registered on an exact date; shared by the daily-limit and bulk-signup rules.

---

## 4. Existing tests

There are only two test files, both under `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/`:

- **`AcceptanceBase.java`** — black-box base (`@SpringBootTest`, `@AutoConfigureMockMvc`, `@Transactional`, `@WithMockUser`). It exercises the single endpoint `POST /api/owners` + `GET /api/owners/{id}`. Contains helpers directly relevant to your topics: `toBusinessDay(LocalDate)` (replicates the weekend/holiday roll), the pinned `HOLIDAYS` set (same 2026 dates), `luhn(...)`, `shaHex(...)`/`sha256hex(...)`, region/timezone/postcode reference maps. Its class Javadoc explicitly notes the membership-number and business-day/per-day rules.

- **`AcceptanceTest.java`** — currently a single test targeting a **fiscal-year** field that does not yet exist in the code:

```java
/** fiscal-year: Move date-derived values to a fiscal-year basis, where the fiscal year starts on 1 July. ... */
@Test
void coreReturnsFiscalYear() throws Exception {
    int id = createOwnerOk(structuredOwner());
    JsonNode n = fetchOwner(id);
    assertTrue(n.get("fiscalYear").asText().matches("FY\\d{2}"));
}
```

Note: I found **no `fiscalYear` field anywhere in `src/main`** (not in `OwnerMapper.java` nor `openapi.yml`). So this test asserts a `fiscalYear` (pattern `FY\d{2}`) that is not yet implemented — it will currently fail. This appears to be the pending task: derive a fiscal-year value (fiscal year starting 1 July) from the registration date and expose it as a `fiscalYear` DTO field, analogous to the existing `-M<YY>` year-segment logic in `membershipNumber`.

---

## 5. Build system and running tests

- **Build system: Maven**, with the wrapper `/home/daniel/sandbox/mvnw` (and `mvnw.cmd`). Root `/home/daniel/sandbox/pom.xml` inherits from `spring-boot-starter-parent`; uses the OfficeFloor Spring Boot 4 starter and the OpenAPI Generator plugin (DTOs like `OwnerDto` are generated at build time — see `readme.md` lines ~203-218).
- **Run tests:** `./mvnw test` (unit/acceptance). Full build incl. DTO generation: `./mvnw clean install` (readme line 218 uses `mvn clean install`). Run the app: `./mvnw spring-boot:run` (readme line 25).
- Test stack: JUnit 5 (`org.junit.jupiter`), Spring MockMvc, `spring-boot-starter-security-test` (`@WithMockUser`), Jackson (`tools.jackson`), Mockito — all declared in `pom.xml`.

To run just the acceptance test: `./mvnw test -Dtest=AcceptanceTest`.

